body: "Follow-up to #305. CodeRabbit's review of 35b3536 left three non-blocking edge cases in `scripts/published-document-links.ts`. The audit should treat Markdown the way GitHub renders it: skip code spans and code blocks, read destinations with nested balanced parentheses, and handle a reference title that starts on the next line. Consider reusing a CommonMark-compliant parser rather than extending the hand-written matcher:\n\n- [scripts/published-document-links.ts:44](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/305#discussion_r4546020638): Exclude code text before checking destinations.\n- [scripts/published-document-links.ts:48](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/305#discussion_r4546020649): Read destinations with nested balanced parentheses.\n- [scripts/published-document-links.ts:49](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/305#discussion_r4546020658): Include a reference title that starts on the next line.\n\nEach fix needs a test that fails on revert."
